te limestone, broken on all sides, including the rear (so not preserving original thickness), now of roughly trapezoidal shape; presumably part of a plaque or stele.\u003C/p>\n                                    \u003Cmaterial ana=\"#material.inorganic.stone.sedimentary_rock.limestone.calcilutite.white.calcare-lucidabile_bianco_tipo-scaglia #material.inorganic.stone.sedimentary_rock.limestone.calcilutite.white.calcare-lucidabile_bianco_lattimusa\" type=\"stone.limestone.polishable.white\" subtype=\"calcare_bianco_tipo-scaglia|calcare_bianco_scaglia\" resp=\"#Coccato\" ref=\"http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/material/lod/66.html\">compact whitish limestone with chonchoidal fracture and veins, likely tipo scaglia (SCA, AMM) (wackestone with foraminifera) (identification based on digital microscopy)\u003C/material>\n                                    \u003CobjectType ana=\"#object.plaque\" ref=\"http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/objtyp/lod/259\">plaque\u003C/objectType>\n                                    \u003Cdimensions>\u003C!--from Arena-->\n                                        \u003Cheight unit=\"cm\">10.5\u003C/height>\n                                        \u003Cwidth unit=\"cm\">11.9\u003C/width>\n                                        \u003Cdepth unit=\"cm\">2.8-3.7\u003C/depth>\n                                    \u003C/dimensions>\n                                \u003C/support>\n                                \u003Ccondition ana=\"#condition.fragment\"/>\n\t\t    \u003C/supportDesc>\n                            \u003ClayoutDesc>\n                                \u003Clayout>\u003Cp>Remains of the right margin of 5 lines of text (the final line poorly preserved); vacat above (11 mm maximum, against an interlinear measurement of 6 mm) suggests this may be the first line of the text.\u003C/p>\n                                    \u003Crs ana=\"#execution.chiselled\" ref=\"http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/writing/lod/1\">chiselled\u003C/rs>\n                                \t\u003Cdamage ana=\"#text_condition.incomplete\"/>\n\t\t\t\u003C/layout>\n                            \u003C/layoutDesc>\n                        \u003C/objectDesc>\n                        \u003ChandDesc>\n                            \u003ChandNote>\u003C!--Arena-->\u003Cp>Arena notes that the quadrangular module of the individual letters is regular, with the combined module of omicron-nu (used as a control across multiple similar fragments) being 9-10mm from centre to centre. Letters with neat terminal serifs, elegantly cut.\u003C/p>\n                                \u003Clocus from=\"line1\" to=\"line5\">Line 1-5\u003C/locus>\n                                \u003Cdimensions type=\"letterHeight\">\n                                    \u003Cheight unit=\"mm\" atLeast=\"8\" atMost=\"8\">8\u003C/height>\n                                \u003C/dimensions>\n                                \u003Clocus from=\"line1\" to=\"line5\">Interlineation\u003C/locus>\n                                \u003Cdimensions type=\"interlinear\">\n                                    \u003Cheight unit=\"mm\" atLeast=\"6\" atMost=\"6\">6\u003C/height>\n                                \u003C/dimensions>\n                            \u003C/handNote>\n                        \u003C/handDesc>\n                    \u003C/physDesc>\n                    \u003Chistory>\n                        \u003Corigin>\n                            \u003CorigPlace>\u003Cregion>Sicilia\u003C/region>\n                                \u003CplaceName type=\"ancient\" ref=\"http://pleiades.stoa.org/places/462225\">Halaesa\u003C/placeName>\t\t\n                                \u003Coffset>near\n                                    \u003CplaceName type=\"modern\" ref=\"http://sws.geonames.org/2525099\">Castel di Tusa\u003C/placeName>\n                                \u003C/offset>\n                            \t\u003Cgeo>37.99907, 14.26197\u003C/geo>\n\t\t\u003C/origPlace>\n                            \u003CorigDate datingMethod=\"#julian\" notBefore-custom=\"-00150\" notAfter-custom=\"-0051\" evidence=\"lettering\">Later 2nd century BCE or early C1 BCE\u003C/origDate>\n                        \u003C/origin>\n                        \u003Cprovenance type=\"found\" subtype=\"discovered\">Found by Francesco Modico in spring 2019, 2 m east of the city walls, in the direction of the Masseria di Salvo\u003Cgeo cert=\"high\">37.9964141,14.2625583\u003C/geo>; now on display in the ecomuseo, in Castel di Tusa.\u003C/provenance>\u003C!-- approx findspot, based on map in Arena 2020 tav.VI -->\n                    \u003Cprovenance type=\"observed\" subtype=\"autopsied\">None\u003C/provenance>\n                        \u003Cacquisition/>\n                    \u003C/history>\n                \u003C/msDesc>\n            \u003C/sourceDesc>\n        \u003C/fileDesc>\n        \u003CencodingDesc>\n             \u003Cp>Encoded following the latest EpiDoc guidelines\u003C/p>\n             \u003Cxi:include href=\"../alists/ISicily-taxonomies.xml\">\n                 \u003Cxi:fallback>\n                     \u003Cp>Taxonomies for ISicily controlled values\u003C/p>\n                 \u003C/xi:fallback>\n             \u003C/xi:include>\n\t  \u003Cxi:include href=\"../alists/charDecl.xml\">\n\t     \u003Cxi:fallback>\n\t       \u003Cp>ISicily glyphs authority list\u003C/p>\n\t     \u003C/xi:fallback>\n\t   \u003C/xi:include>\n         \u003C/encodingDesc>\n        \u003CprofileDesc>\n            \u003CcalendarDesc>\n                \u003Ccalendar xml:id=\"julian\">\n                    \u003Cp>Julian Calendar\u003C/p>\n                \u003C/calendar>\n            \u003C/calendarDesc>\n            \u003ClangUsage>\n                \u003Clanguage ident=\"en\">English\u003C/language>\n                \u003Clanguage ident=\"it\">Italian\u003C/language>\n                \u003Clanguage ident=\"grc\">Ancient Greek\u003C/language>\n                \u003Clanguage ident=\"la\">Latin\u003C/language>\n                \u003Clanguage ident=\"he\">Hebrew\u003C/language>\n                \u003Clanguage ident=\"phn\">Phoenician\u003C/language>\n                \u003Clanguage ident=\"xpu\">Punic\u003C/language>\n                \u003Clanguage ident=\"osc\">Oscan\u003C/language>\n                \u003Clanguage ident=\"xly\">Elymian\u003C/language>\n                \u003Clanguage ident=\"scx\">Sikel\u003C/language>\n                \u003Clanguage ident=\"sxc\">Sikan\u003C/language>\n            \u003C/langUsage>\n            \u003CtextClass>\n                \u003Ckeywords scheme=\"https://ontology.inscriptiones.org/type_of_inscription\">\n                    \u003Cterm ana=\"#function.honorific\" ref=\"https://ontology.inscriptiones.org/type_of_inscription/Honorific\" cert=\"low\">honorific\u003C/term>\n                \u003C/keywords>\n            \u003C/textClass>\n        \u003C/profileDesc>\n        \u003CrevisionDesc status=\"edited\">\n            \u003ClistChange>\n                \u003Cchange when=\"2022-09-23\" who=\"#JP\">Jonathan Prag created file from template based on editio princeps of Arena 2020\u003C/change>\n                \u003Cchange when=\"2026-03-18\" who=\"#JP\">Jonathan Prag added text\u003C/change>\n             \u003C/listChange>\n        \u003C/revisionDesc>\n    \u003C/teiHeader>\n    \u003Cfacsimile>\u003Csurface/>\u003C!-- \n        \u003Csurface type=\"front\">\n            \u003Cgraphic n=\"screen\" url=\"ISic001695_tiled.tif\" height=\"3680px\" width=\"5520px\">\n                \u003Cdesc>I.Sicily with the permission of the Assessorato Regionale dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana - Dipartimento dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana\u003C/desc>\n            \u003C/graphic>\n            \u003Cgraphic n=\"print\" url=\"ISic001695.jpg\" height=\"3680px\" width=\"5520px\">\n                \u003Cdesc>I.Sicily with the permission of the Assessorato Regionale dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana - Dipartimento dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana\u003C/desc>\n            \u003C/graphic>\n         \u003C/surface> -->\n         \u003C/facsimile>\n    \u003Ctext>\n        \u003Cbody>\n            \u003Cdiv type=\"edition\" subtype=\"primary\" xml:space=\"preserve\" xml:lang=\"grc\" resp=\"#JP\">\n                \u003Cab>\n                    \u003Clb n=\"1\"/>\u003Cgap reason=\"lost\" extent=\"unknown\" unit=\"character\"/>\u003Corig>ΑΤΑΙΕ\u003C/orig>\n                    \u003Clb n=\"2\"/>\u003Corig>ΣΑΔΕΚΑ\u003Csupplied reason=\"lost\" cert=\"low\">Ι\u003C/supplied>\u003C/orig>\n                    \u003Clb n=\"3\"/>\u003Corig>ΙΑΝΑΤΑ\u003C/orig>\n                    \u003Clb n=\"4\"/>\u003Cgap reason=\"lost\" extent=\"unknown\" unit=\"character\"/> \u003Csupplied reason=\"lost\">καὶ\u003C/supplied> \u003Csupplied reason=\"lost\">τοῖς\u003C/supplied> \u003Csupplied reason=\"lost\">ἐ\u003C/supplied>\u003Cunclear>γ\u003C/unclear>γόνοις\n                    \u003Clb n=\"5\"/>\u003Cgap reason=\"lost\" extent=\"unknown\" unit=\"character\"/>\u003Corig>\u003Cunclear>Ν\u003C/unclear>Τ\u003Cunclear>ΑΣ\u003C/unclear>\u003C/orig>\n                \u003C/ab>\n            \u003C/div>\n            \u003Cdiv type=\"apparatus\">\n                \u003ClistApp>\n                    \u003Capp>\u003Cnote>Text of Arena 2020\u003C/note>\u003C/app>\n                    \u003Capp loc=\"2\">\u003Cnote>As Arena notes, the break at the end of the line need not conceal a letter and the numeral δεκα is just as possible as κα[ι]\u003C/note>\u003C/app>\n                \u003C/listApp>\n              \u003C/div>\n            \u003Cdiv type=\"translation\">\n                \u003Cp>\u003C!--translation(s) - add @xml:lang for 'en' or 'it' to div-->\u003C/p>\n            \u003C/div>\n            \u003Cdiv type=\"commentary\">\n                \u003Cp>The apparent presence of [--ἐ]γγόνοις in line 4 strongly suggests an honorific decree (so Arena).\u003C/p>\n            \u003C/div>\n            \u003Cdiv type=\"bibliography\">\n                \u003ClistBibl type=\"edition\">\n                   \u003Cbibl>\n                        \u003Cauthor>Arena\u003C/author>\n                        \u003Cdate>2020\u003C/date>\n                        \u003CcitedRange>81-83 no. 6\u003C/citedRange>\n                        \u003Cptr target=\"https://www.zotero.org/groups/382445/items/KAIR5ZLR\"/>\n                    \u003Cref target=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002404\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002404\u003C/ref>\u003C/bibl>\n                \u003C/listBibl>\n\t   \u003ClistBibl type=\"discussion\">\n\t       \u003Cbibl>\n\t       \u003C/bibl>\n\t   \u003C/listBibl>\n            \u003C/div>\n        \u003C/body>\n    \u003C/text>\n\u003C/TEI>\n"],"uses":{"params":["slug"]}}]}
